s avifauna, particularly its large flocks of migratory waterfowl and wading birds. The park is 391 kilometres (243\u00a0mi) southeast of Colombo on Sri Lanka's southeastern coast. Kumana is contiguous with Yala National Park, and was formerly known as Yala East National Park and was renamed to its present name in 2006.", "extract_html": "<p><b>Kumana National Park</b> in Sri Lanka is renowned for its avifauna, particularly its large flocks of migratory waterfowl and wading birds. The park is 391 kilometres (243\u00a0mi) southeast of Colombo on Sri Lanka's southeastern coast. Kumana is contiguous with Yala National Park, and was formerly known as <b>Yala East National Park</b> and was renamed to its present name in 2006.</p>"}